      "kind": "code",
      "instructions": "Write a short Python script that runs inside Blender:\n1. Load ~/Music/track.wav as a sound strip.\n2. Use `bpy.ops.graph.sound_bake()` with `low=20`, `high=250` (bass range) to bake the sound to a dummy Empty object's location X channel.\n3. Rename the Empty to `BassDriver` and keep the baked F‑curve.\n4. Save the Blender file as `bass_visualizer.blend` (or return the name of the Empty and the action name for later steps).\nOutput: the exact script text (no extra explanation) and the names `BassDriver` and `BassAction` used.",
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "title": "Create a ring of 32 cubes",
      "kind": "code",
      "instructions": "Provide a Blender Python snippet that:\n1. Creates 32 mesh cubes named `Cube_001` … `Cube_032`.\n2. Positions them in a perfect circle of radius 5 units on the XY‑plane (Z = 0), equally spaced (angle = 360/32 degrees).\n3. Parents all cubes to an Empty called `RingCtrl` for easy manipulation.\n4. Saves the script and mentions that the script must be run after step s1 (no direct dependency on its data).\nOutput: the full script text.",
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "title": "Add emission material driven by bass",
      "kind": "code",
      "instructions": "Write a Blender Python script that:\n1. Creates a new material `BassGlow` using Principled BSDF with Emission node.\n2. Connects Emission Strength to a driver that reads the baked F‑curve from `BassDriver` (the X location channel).\n   - Use `driver.type = 'AVERAGE'` and set `driver.targets[0].id = bpy.data.objects['BassDriver']` and `driver.targets[0].data_path = 'location.x'`.\n3. Assigns `BassGlow` to all cubes `Cube_001` … `Cube_032`.\n4. Ensures the driver multiplies the raw value by a factor (e.g., 5) for visible intensity.\nOutput: the complete script text.\nDepends_on: [\"s1\", \"s2\"]",
      "depends_on": ["s1", "s2"]
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "title": "Animate a slow camera push‑in",
      "kind": "code",
      "instructions": "Provide a Blender Python snippet that:\n1. Adds a camera named `Cam` positioned at (0, -12, 3) looking at the origin.\n2. Inserts a keyframe for location at frame 1.\n3. Inserts a keyframe for location at the last frame of the audio (use `bpy.context.scene.frame_end` which should be set to the length of the wav after baking).\n   - Target location at the last frame: (0, -4, 3) (a slow push‑in).\n4. Sets interpolation to linear for both keyframes.\nOutput: the full script text.",
      "depends_on": ["s1"]
    },
