      "id": "s5",
      "title": "Set up compositor bloom (Glare) node",
      "kind": "code",
      "instructions": "Write a Blender Python script that:\n1. Enables `use_nodes` for the compositor.\n2. Clears existing nodes.\n3. Adds a Render Layers node, a Glare node (type='FOG_GLOW', mix=0.5, size=9), and a Composite node.\n4. Links Render Layers → Glare → Composite.\n5. Sets the render engine to `CYCLES` (or `EEVEE` with bloom disabled, but compositor bloom used).\nOutput: the complete script text.\nDepends_on: [] (can run after scene creation).",
      "depends_on": []
    }
  ]
}

{
  "title": "GLB Contact Sheet Generator",
  "kind": "blender",
  "summary": "A Blender script that scans a folder for all .glb files, imports each model, arranges them on a grid with a text label of the filename beneath each model, sets up an orthographic camera to frame the whole grid, and renders a single contact sheet image.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "title": "Collect GLB file list",
      "kind": "code",
      "instructions": "Write a Python function `list_glb_files(folder_path: str) -> List[str]` that returns a sorted list of absolute file paths for every `.glb` file in `folder_path`. The function should ignore sub‑folders and non‑GLB files. Output the list as a JSON array to stdout.",
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "title": "Compute grid layout",
      "kind": "code",
      "instructions": "Create a Python function `compute_grid_positions(count: int, spacing: float = 2.0) -> List[Tuple[int, int]]` that returns a list of (row, col) tuples for each item, filling rows first. Choose the number of columns as the ceiling of sqrt(count) and rows accordingly. Output the list of tuples as JSON.",
      "depends_on": ["s1"]
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "title": "Import models and add labels",
      "kind": "blender",
      "instructions": "Write a Blender Python script that:\n1. Receives the JSON outputs of `s1` (file list) and `s2` (grid positions).\n2. For each .glb file, imports it with `bpy.ops.import_scene.gltf(filepath=...)`.\n3. Moves the imported collection to `(col * spacing, -row * spacing, 0)` where `spacing` is 2.5 units (you may adjust).\n4. Creates a `bpy.data.curves.new` text object with the base filename (no extension) placed directly below the model at `z = -0.2`.\n5. Parents the text to the model collection for easy cleanup.\n6. Stores all created objects in a master collection named \"ContactSheet\".\nThe script should write a success message and the names of all created objects to stdout.\n",
      "depends_on": ["s1", "s2"]
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "title": "Setup orthographic camera",
      "kind": "blender",
      "instructions": "Extend the Blender script to:\n1. Add a new camera object named `ContactCam`.\n2. Set its type to `ORTHO` and position it directly above the grid looking down the -Z axis (`rotation_euler = (radians(90), 0, 0)`).\n3. Compute the required orthographic scale to frame all objects plus a small margin (e.g., 10%). Use the bounding box of the \"ContactSheet\" collection.\n4. Set the camera as the scene's active camera.\n5. Output the final camera location, rotation, and ortho_scale as JSON.\n",
      "depends_on": ["s3"]
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "title": "Render contact sheet image",
      "kind": "blender",
      "instructions": "Finalize the script to:\n1. Set render engine to `CYCLES` (or `BLENDER_EEVEE`).\n2. Set resolution to 1920x1080 (or based on grid size: columns * 400, rows * 400).\n3. Enable transparent background if desired.\n4. Render a single frame to `contact_sheet.png` in the same folder as the script.\n5. Print the file path of the rendered image.\nThe script should be runnable from the command line with `blender --background --python script.py -- <folder_path>`.\n",
      "depends_on": ["s4"]
    }
  ]
}

